    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0263",
      "reading_order": 319,
      "section": "3.4.3 LBS (Load Bus Synchronization)",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 77.904,
        "t": 308.4576629101563,
        "r": 541.52944,
        "b": 236.58610136319498
      },
      "content": "Dual bus system uses LBS cable option to realize the synchronous output of two independent (or parallel) UPS system. One of the systems is master system and the other one is slave system. The operation mode of dual bus system includes the operation of master / slave system in inversion or bypass  mode.  The  wiring  diagram  between  synchronous  controller  and  stand-alone  or  parallel system is as shown in Figure 3-21 and 3-22;",
      "section_id": "sec_3_4_3",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3_4",
